  "question": {
    "text": "A police car moving at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, chases a motorcyclist. The policeman sounds his horn at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>, while both of them move towards a stationary siren of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>160</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. If it is given that the motorcyclist does not observe any beats then, calculate the speed (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)&nbsp;of the motorcyclist round off to two decimal places? [speed of sound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>330</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"
  },
